* 00 thermal-voltage check (not a comparison deck): what Vt = kT/q does ngspice use at temp = tnom = 26.85 C?
* A 1 mA current into an ideal diode (Is 1e-14, N 1, Rs 0) gives V = Vt*ln(1 + I/Is); the control block solves for Vt.
* NODE uses Vt = 25.852 mV (DESIGN 3.3, T fixed at 300 K).
.include common.inc
.model DCHK D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
I1 0 a DC 1m
D1 a 0 DCHK
.control
op
let vt_mV = 1000*v(a)/ln(1 + 1m/1e-14)
set numdgt=8
echo "VT-CHECK ngspice_Vt_mV = $&vt_mV (CODATA-2018 kT/q at 300 K = 25.85200 mV; NODE = 25.852 mV)"
.endc
.end
